          "content": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( -90 \\le n \\le 90 \\) and \\(\\sin n^\\circ = \\sin 419^\\circ\\), we need to use the periodic and symmetric properties of the sine function. The sine function is periodic with period \\(360^\\circ\\), and it has the property that \\(\\sin(\\theta) = \\sin(180^\\circ - \\theta)\\) and \\(\\sin(\\theta) = \\sin(180^\\circ + \\theta)\\).\n\nFirst, we reduce \\(419^\\circ\\) to an angle between \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(360^\\circ\\):\n\\[\n419^\\circ = 420^\\circ - 1^\\circ = 360^\\circ + 60^\\circ - 1^\\circ = 360^\\circ - 1^\\circ.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin(419^\\circ) = \\sin(360^\\circ - 1^\\circ)\\), and using the identity \\(\\sin(360^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\sin(\\theta)\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\sin(419^\\circ) = \\sin(360^\\circ - 1^\\circ) = -\\sin(1^\\circ).\n\\]\nThus, \\(\\sin 419^\\circ = -\\sin 1^\\circ\\). We need to find an angle \\(n\\) such that \\(\\sin n^\\circ = -\\sin 1^\\circ\\). Using the identity \\(\\sin(-\\theta) = -\\sin(\\theta)\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\sin n^\\circ = -\\sin 1^\\circ = \\sin(-1^\\circ).\n\\]\nTherefore, \\(n = -1\\) is a solution. We need to check if there are any other solutions in the range \\(-90^\\circ \\le n \\le 90^\\circ\\). The general solution for \\(\\sin n^\\circ = -\\sin 1^\\circ\\) is:\n\\[\nn = -1 + 360k \\quad \\text{or} \\quad n = 180 - (-1) + 360k = 181 + 360k,\n\\]\nfor any integer \\(k\\). We need to find the values of \\(k\\) such that \\(n\\) lies in the range \\(-90^\\circ \\le n \\le 90^\\circ\\).\n\nFor \\(n = -1 + 360k\\):\n\\[\n-90 \\le -1 + 360k \\le 90 \\implies -89 \\le 360k \\le 91 \\implies -\\frac{89}{360} \\le k \\le \\frac{91}{360}.\n\\]\nThe only integer \\(k\\) in this range is \\(k = 0\\), so \\(n = -1\\).\n\nFor \\(n = 181 + 360k\\):\n\\[\n-90 \\le 181 + 360k \\le 90 \\implies -171 \\le 360k \\le -91 \\implies -\\frac{171}{360} \\le k \\le -\\frac{91}{360}.\n\\]\nThe only integer \\(k\\) in this range is \\(k = -1\\), so \\(n = 181 - 360 = -181\\), but this is not in the range \\(-90 \\le n \\le 90\\).\n\nTherefore, the only solution in the range \\(-90 \\le n \\le 90\\) is \\(n = -1\\). The answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]",
